From e17641646746e7044d13c7e3698869506a43225e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:17:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Grand Exchange partial fills and 4-hour buy limits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem:
The minimal GE fills every offer at once and has no buy limits, so any
quantity of an item can be bought straight away.

Change:
- Fills come in up to four parts (2 ticks after Confirm, then every 5
  ticks), each sent as a partial UPDATE_STOCKMARKET_SLOT with a "Grand
  Exchange: Bought/Sold n / total x Item." line, and "Grand Exchange:
  Finished buying/selling n x Item." at the end.
- Buys count against the item's buy limit (enum ge_buy_limits, 64441); an
  offer over the limit stays open until the 4-hour window that began with the
  first item bought ends. Selling has no limit.
- Limits are tracked in 16 per-player entries (varps 64005-64052); a live
  window is never dropped. When all 16 hold live windows, a buy of a 17th
  limited item waits until one ends.
- Offers keep filling while the player is logged out: the logout minute is
  kept (varp ge_logout_minute, 64054) and the login applies every fill since
  then, restarting limit windows at the minute the old ones ran out, before
  it sends the slots, so the slots show the progress and collection works at
  once.

Tests:
GrandExchangeScriptTest: partial fills (3 of 10 after the first step), abort
of a partly filled buy, a buy over the limit waiting for the 4-hour window, a
full set of limit trackers never dropping a live window, offers filling while
logged out with limit windows restarting on time.

Data sources:
OSRS Wiki "Grand Exchange/Buying limits" (4 hours from the first purchase,
no limit on selling); limit values generated from the wiki's
Module:GELimits/data.json (17 October 2026); OSRS Wiki "Grand Exchange"
intro (traders do not need to wait at the GE for trades to finish).

Caveats:
- The fill pacing (four parts, 2/5 ticks, a 1-minute recheck for
  limit-blocked offers) and the chat line wording are unsourced.
- No chat line at login for offers that changed while logged out (the
  wording is not on the wiki); no pause of offers after several days logged
  out.
- Connected limits (e.g. potion doses) are not shared.
- At most 16 limited items in live windows at once (OSRS has no cap).

